      "text": "Change data capture\n(CDC)\nChange data capture\n(CDC) reads a database's\nown change log. It turns\neach committed insert,\nupdate, and delete into\nan event. The source\ntables keep their\nschema: CDC adds no\ntriggers and no columns.\n\nThe result is a stream\nof changes, not a copy\nof the table. A row that\nchanges three times\nproduces three events,\nand a delete produces an\nevent too.\n\nThe usual alternatives\nsee less. A scheduled\nfull extract copies\nwhole tables, so it is\nheavy and always late. A\nquery for rows changed\nsince the last run needs\na reliable last-changed\ncolumn, and it never\nsees a deleted row.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-5c8705183cba",
      "originalText": "Change data capture (CDC)\nChange data capture (CDC) reads a database's own change log. It turns each committed insert, update, and delete into an event. The source tables keep their schema: CDC adds no triggers and no columns.\n\nThe result is a stream of changes, not a copy of the table. A row that changes three times produces three events, and a delete produces an event too.\n\nThe usual alternatives see less. A scheduled full extract copies whole tables, so it is heavy and always late. A query for rows changed since the last run needs a reliable last-changed column, and it never sees a deleted row.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "change-data-capture"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 7855446339,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "node-8aabe710ae6e",
