    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 3202581470,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-8aabe710ae6e",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1094.4,
      "y": 386.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 126.0,
      "height": 2257.5,
      "seed": 724426,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Schema\nregistry\nA schema\nregistry is a\nsmall service\nnext to Kafka\nthat stores\nthe schema of\neach topic's\nrecords. A\nschema lists\nevery field\nand its type.\nThe registry\nkeeps each\nschema under a\nsubject,\nusually named\nafter the\ntopic, such as\nreadings-value\nfor the values\nof topic\nreadings. Each\nversion gets a\nnumeric ID.\n\nA message\ncarries only\nthat ID, not\nthe schema. In\nthis pattern,\nmessages use\nAvro, a\ncompact binary\nformat. Each\nAvro message\nstarts with a\n5-byte header:\na zero byte,\nthen the\nschema ID in 4\nbytes. The\nreader fetches\nthe schema for\nthat ID once,\ncaches it, and\ndecodes the\nrest. So\nmessages stay\nsmall, and the\nsink knows\neach field's\ntype. It needs\nthose types to\nwrite Parquet,\na column-based\nfile format\nwith a type\nfor every\ncolumn.\n\nFor example, a\nmessage starts\nwith the bytes\n0, 0, 0, 0, 7.\nThe sink asks\nthe registry\nfor schema 7\nand learns\nthat id is a\nlong, truck is\nan int, and\nend is a\ntimestamp that\ncan be empty.\nIt then writes\nthose values\ninto columns\nof those\ntypes.\n\nThe registry\nalso guards\nchanges.\nBefore it\naccepts a new\nversion, it\nchecks the\nversion\nagainst the\nolder ones\nwith a\ncompatibility\nrule. Under FU\nLL_TRANSITIVE,\na new version\nmust work for\nreaders and\nwriters of\nevery earlier\nversion.\nAdding an\noptional field\npasses.\nChanging a\nfield's type,\nsuch as from\nnumber to\ntext, fails,\nand the\nproducer gets\nan error\ninstead of\nsending the\nchange. So the\nregistry\ndecides which\nschema changes\ncan ever reach\nthe table.\n\nKarapace is an\nopen-source\nschema\nregistry that\nspeaks the\nsame API as\nConfluent's.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-8aabe710ae6e",
      "originalText": "Schema registry\nA schema registry is a small service next to Kafka that stores the schema of each topic's records. A schema lists every field and its type. The registry keeps each schema under a subject, usually named after the topic, such as readings-value for the values of topic readings. Each version gets a numeric ID.\n\nA message carries only that ID, not the schema. In this pattern, messages use Avro, a compact binary format. Each Avro message starts with a 5-byte header: a zero byte, then the schema ID in 4 bytes. The reader fetches the schema for that ID once, caches it, and decodes the rest. So messages stay small, and the sink knows each field's type. It needs those types to write Parquet, a column-based file format with a type for every column.\n\nFor example, a message starts with the bytes 0, 0, 0, 0, 7. The sink asks the registry for schema 7 and learns that id is a long, truck is an int, and end is a timestamp that can be empty. It then writes those values into columns of those types.\n\nThe registry also guards changes. Before it accepts a new version, it checks the version against the older ones with a compatibility rule. Under FULL_TRANSITIVE, a new version must work for readers and writers of every earlier version. Adding an optional field passes. Changing a field's type, such as from number to text, fails, and the producer gets an error instead of sending the change. So the registry decides which schema changes can ever reach the table.\n\nKarapace is an open-source schema registry that speaks the same API as Confluent's.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "schema-registry"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
