    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 7910142120,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-209c77b42a5a",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1094.4,
      "y": 630.5,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 100.80000000000001,
      "height": 1662.5,
      "seed": 88079,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "REST catalog\nA REST\ncatalog is\nan Iceberg\ncatalog that\nclients\nreach\nthrough the\nopen Iceberg\nREST API\nover HTTPS.\nLike every\ncatalog, it\nmaps each\ntable name\nto the\ntable's\ncurrent\nmetadata\nfile. The\n[Iceberg map\n](../../iceb\nerg/iceberg.\nmd) explains\nthat role.\nBecause the\nAPI is a\nstandard,\nany engine\nwith an\nIceberg\nclient can\nuse it.\nHere, the\nsink writes\nthrough it,\nand\nSnowflake\nreads\nthrough it.\n\nThe catalog\nalso\ncontrols\naccess. Each\nclient signs\nin as a\nprincipal, a\ncatalog\nuser, with\nOAuth (open \nauthorizatio\nn) client\ncredentials,\na standard\nsign-in\nmethod for\nprograms.\nRoles then\ndecide what\neach\nprincipal\nmay do: the\nsink's\nprincipal\ncan change\ntable\ncontents,\nand\nSnowflake's\nprincipal\ncan only\nread. If two\nwriters\ncommit to\none table at\nthe same\ntime, the\ncatalog\naccepts one\ncommit and\nrejects the\nother, which\nthen\nretries.\n\nSnowflake\nOpen Catalog\nis a managed\nversion of\nApache\nPolaris, an\nopen-source\nREST\ncatalog.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-209c77b42a5a",
      "originalText": "REST catalog\nA REST catalog is an Iceberg catalog that clients reach through the open Iceberg REST API over HTTPS. Like every catalog, it maps each table name to the table's current metadata file. The [Iceberg map](../../iceberg/iceberg.md) explains that role. Because the API is a standard, any engine with an Iceberg client can use it. Here, the sink writes through it, and Snowflake reads through it.\n\nThe catalog also controls access. Each client signs in as a principal, a catalog user, with OAuth (open authorization) client credentials, a standard sign-in method for programs. Roles then decide what each principal may do: the sink's principal can change table contents, and Snowflake's principal can only read. If two writers commit to one table at the same time, the catalog accepts one commit and rejects the other, which then retries.\n\nSnowflake Open Catalog is a managed version of Apache Polaris, an open-source REST catalog.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "rest-catalog"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 3652123544,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "node-b44c8e2d8508",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1082.4,
      "y": 712.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "#F8FAFC",
      "width": 141.60000000000002,
      "height": 41.5,
      "seed": 174962,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3,
        "value": 8
      },
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "type": "text",
