    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1593013347,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-38d1a13ca669",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1094.4,
      "y": 793.5,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 252.0,
      "height": 1050.0,
      "seed": 525878,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Valid-through timestamp\n(VTTS)\nThe valid-through timestamp\n(VTTS) is a watermark: a time\nup to which the data is\ncomplete. The sink writes it\ninto each commit's snapshot\nsummary, a small set of notes\nstored with every snapshot,\nunder the key kafka.connect.v\nalid-through-ts.\n\nFor each topic partition, the\nsink takes the latest record\ntimestamp that the commit\nincludes. The VTTS is the\nearliest of those values,\nbecause the slowest partition\ndecides what is complete. So\nevery record with a Kafka\ntimestamp at or below the\nVTTS is already committed.\n\nFor example, a commit covers\nthree partitions whose latest\nrecords are from 10:04:58,\n10:04:59, and 10:03:10. The\nVTTS is 10:03:10. A model\nfilters on a column that\nholds each record's Kafka\ntimestamp, and it stops at\n10:03:10. A later commit\ncannot add a row at or below\nthat time, except after a\nreplay of old records. A row\ntimestamp alone gives no such\npromise, because rows become\nvisible one commit at a time.\n\nThree details matter in\npractice. The VTTS is\nmissing, not zero, after a\npartial commit, one that\ntimed out before every task\nanswered. It is also missing\nwhen a partition sent nothing\nin that round. One stuck\npartition holds the whole\ntable's VTTS back, which\nlooks the same as no new\ndata. And the VTTS only moves\nforward when the broker\nstamps each record with its\nown clock (LogAppendTime).\nWith the producer's clock, it\ncan move back. In Snowflake, \nICEBERG_TABLE_SNAPSHOT_REFRES\nH_HISTORY returns each\nsnapshot's summary, so a\nquery can read the VTTS.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-38d1a13ca669",
      "originalText": "Valid-through timestamp (VTTS)\nThe valid-through timestamp (VTTS) is a watermark: a time up to which the data is complete. The sink writes it into each commit's snapshot summary, a small set of notes stored with every snapshot, under the key kafka.connect.valid-through-ts.\n\nFor each topic partition, the sink takes the latest record timestamp that the commit includes. The VTTS is the earliest of those values, because the slowest partition decides what is complete. So every record with a Kafka timestamp at or below the VTTS is already committed.\n\nFor example, a commit covers three partitions whose latest records are from 10:04:58, 10:04:59, and 10:03:10. The VTTS is 10:03:10. A model filters on a column that holds each record's Kafka timestamp, and it stops at 10:03:10. A later commit cannot add a row at or below that time, except after a replay of old records. A row timestamp alone gives no such promise, because rows become visible one commit at a time.\n\nThree details matter in practice. The VTTS is missing, not zero, after a partial commit, one that timed out before every task answered. It is also missing when a partition sent nothing in that round. One stuck partition holds the whole table's VTTS back, which looks the same as no new data. And the VTTS only moves forward when the broker stamps each record with its own clock (LogAppendTime). With the producer's clock, it can move back. In Snowflake, ICEBERG_TABLE_SNAPSHOT_REFRESH_HISTORY returns each snapshot's summary, so a query can read the VTTS.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "valid-through-timestamp"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 8988515643,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "node-9947d5412704",
