    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 3442339787,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-86398aa18ef6",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1932.4,
      "y": 1119.5,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 76.0,
      "height": 2275.0,
      "seed": 264900,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Outputs\nThe\nconnector\nwrites\none Kafka\ntopic per\ncaptured\ntable.\nEach\nrecord's\nkey is\nthe row's\nprimary\nkey. Its\nvalue is\nan\nenvelope\nwith\nthree\nmain\nparts:\nthe opera\ntion, the\nrow\nbefore\nand after\nthe\nchange,\nand\nsource\ndetails.\nThe\nsource\ndetails\ninclude\nthe table\nname and\nthe\ncommit\ntime. Key\nand value\nare both\nAvro,\nwith\ntheir\nschemas\nin the\nschema\nregistry.\n\nThe\noperation\ncodes are\nc\n(insert),\nu\n(update),\nd\n(delete),\nand r (a\nrow read\nduring a \nsnapshot)\n. After a\ndelete,\nthe\nconnector\nalso\nsends a t\nombstone:\na record\nwith the\nsame key\nand an\nempty\nvalue.\n\nFor\nexample,\na down\nevent for\ntruck 104\nstarts at\n08:00\nwith no\nend time.\nAt 09:30,\nsomeone\nrecords\nthe end\ntime, and\nthe\nconnector\nsends\nthis\nrecord:\n\n| Part |\nValue |\n| --- |\n--- |\n| key |\nid 7001 |\n| op | u\n|\n| before\n| id\n7001,\ntruck\n104,\nstart\n08:00,\nend empty\n|\n| after |\nid 7001,\ntruck\n104,\nstart\n08:00,\nend 09:30\n|\n| source\n| table d\nown_event\n,\ncommitted\nat\n09:30:02\n|",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-86398aa18ef6",
      "originalText": "Outputs\nThe connector writes one Kafka topic per captured table. Each record's key is the row's primary key. Its value is an envelope with three main parts: the operation, the row before and after the change, and source details. The source details include the table name and the commit time. Key and value are both Avro, with their schemas in the schema registry.\n\nThe operation codes are c (insert), u (update), d (delete), and r (a row read during a snapshot). After a delete, the connector also sends a tombstone: a record with the same key and an empty value.\n\nFor example, a down event for truck 104 starts at 08:00 with no end time. At 09:30, someone records the end time, and the connector sends this record:\n\n| Part | Value |\n| --- | --- |\n| key | id 7001 |\n| op | u |\n| before | id 7001, truck 104, start 08:00, end empty |\n| after | id 7001, truck 104, start 08:00, end 09:30 |\n| source | table down_event, committed at 09:30:02 |",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "cdc-outputs"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 6520138203,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "node-773265b8d445",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1920.4,
      "y": 1201.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
