      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Outputs\nThe sink\nproduces\nParquet\ndata\nfiles and\nmanifest\nfiles in\nS3, and\none\ncommit in\nthe\ncatalog\nper\ncommit\ninterval.\nThe first\nrecord\nfor a\ntable\nthat does\nnot exist\nyet also\ncreates\nthat\ntable in\nthe\ncatalog.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-2c93aea7f37d",
      "originalText": "Outputs\nThe sink produces Parquet data files and manifest files in S3, and one commit in the catalog per commit interval. The first record for a table that does not exist yet also creates that table in the catalog.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "sink-outputs"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 4450421011,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "node-4c00dd0cb32c",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1912.0,
      "y": 1934.5,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "#F8FAFC",
      "width": 141.60000000000002,
      "height": 41.5,
      "seed": 634857,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3,
        "value": 8
      },
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "text-4c00dd0cb32c"
        },
        {
          "id": "edge-a894e3b184a7",
          "type": "arrow"
        },
        {
          "id": "edge-e05d524e48b9",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "sink-under-the-hood"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 3814706761,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-4c00dd0cb32c",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1924.0,
      "y": 1934.5,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 117.60000000000002,
      "height": 2817.5,
      "seed": 534742,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Under the hood\nThe sink runs\nas several\ntasks that\nread the\ntopics in\nparallel. Each\ntask keeps\nwriting\nrecords into\nParquet files,\nbut the sink\ncommits them\nonly on a\ntimer. One\ntask also acts\nas the\ncoordinator.\n\nEvery commit\ninterval, the\ncoordinator\nsends a\nstart-commit\nmessage on the\ncontrol topic.\nThis is a\nsmall Kafka\ntopic that\nonly this\nconnector\nuses. Each\ntask answers\nwith the files\nit wrote since\nthe last\ncommit. When\nevery task has\nanswered, the\ncoordinator\ncommits all of\nthose files in\none snapshot.\n\nThe\ncoordinator\nwaits only\nuntil the\ncommit\ntimeout. Then\nit commits\nwhatever has\narrived, and\nit logs the\ncommit as\ncomplete even\nwhen files are\nmissing.\n\nFor example,\nsuppose the\ncoordinator's\nown task\nanswers in\nunder a\nsecond, and\nthe other\ntasks need 21\nto 48 seconds.\nWith a\n20-second\ntimeout, every\ncommit holds\nonly the\ncoordinator's\nown files. A\n90-second\ntimeout\nincludes every\ntask, and it\nstill fits\nwell inside a\n5-minute\ncommit\ninterval.\n\nThe control\ntopic must\nhave exactly\none partition.\nIf two\nconnectors\nshare one\ncontrol topic,\ntheir\ncoordinators\nmix up each\nother's\nmessages, and\nneither\nfinishes a\ncommit.\n\nWith\nauto-create on\n(iceberg.table\ns.auto-create-\nenabled), the\nsink creates a\nmissing table\nwhen the first\nrecord for it\narrives. It\nmust wait for\nthat record,\nbecause the\ntable's\ncolumns come\nfrom the\nrecord's\nschema. So the\nfirst record\nsets the\ncolumns, and\nit should be a\nreal record,\nnot a test.\nWith schema\nevolution on (\niceberg.tables\n.evolve-schema\n-enabled),\nlater records\ncan add\ncolumns. A\nrenamed field\narrives as a\nnew column,\nand the old\ncolumn stays.\n\nMake sure the\nnamespace\nexists before\nthe first\nrecord\narrives. If\nthe sink\ncannot create\nit, the first\nrecord makes\nthe sink's\ntasks fail.\nThe [Kafka\nConnect sink g\nuide](https://\niceberg.apache\n.org/docs/late\nst/kafka-conne\nct/) lists\nboth settings.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-4c00dd0cb32c",
      "originalText": "Under the hood\nThe sink runs as several tasks that read the topics in parallel. Each task keeps writing records into Parquet files, but the sink commits them only on a timer. One task also acts as the coordinator.\n\nEvery commit interval, the coordinator sends a start-commit message on the control topic. This is a small Kafka topic that only this connector uses. Each task answers with the files it wrote since the last commit. When every task has answered, the coordinator commits all of those files in one snapshot.\n\nThe coordinator waits only until the commit timeout. Then it commits whatever has arrived, and it logs the commit as complete even when files are missing.\n\nFor example, suppose the coordinator's own task answers in under a second, and the other tasks need 21 to 48 seconds. With a 20-second timeout, every commit holds only the coordinator's own files. A 90-second timeout includes every task, and it still fits well inside a 5-minute commit interval.\n\nThe control topic must have exactly one partition. If two connectors share one control topic, their coordinators mix up each other's messages, and neither finishes a commit.\n\nWith auto-create on (iceberg.tables.auto-create-enabled), the sink creates a missing table when the first record for it arrives. It must wait for that record, because the table's columns come from the record's schema. So the first record sets the columns, and it should be a real record, not a test. With schema evolution on (iceberg.tables.evolve-schema-enabled), later records can add columns. A renamed field arrives as a new column, and the old column stays.\n\nMake sure the namespace exists before the first record arrives. If the sink cannot create it, the first record makes the sink's tasks fail. The [Kafka Connect sink guide](https://iceberg.apache.org/docs/latest/kafka-connect/) lists both settings.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "sink-under-the-hood"
      }
    },
